Install `requests`.
`cp .env.example .env` and fill in WB_TOKEN.
Run with `./run.sh`.
Final report in `data/report.csv`.
Logs in `data/*/log`.

Dashboard (Django):
`uv venv .venv && VIRTUAL_ENV=.venv uv pip install -r requirements.txt`.
Add DJANGO_* settings from `.env.example` to `.env` (DJANGO_DEBUG=1 for local use).
`.venv/bin/python manage.py migrate`, then `.venv/bin/python manage.py runserver`.
Create a user: `.venv/bin/python manage.py createsuperuser` (more users at http://127.0.0.1:8000/admin/).
Open http://127.0.0.1:8000 and log in. The page picks up new runs of `./run.sh` automatically.

Docker:
`cp .env.example .env`, fill in WB_TOKEN, DJANGO_SECRET_KEY, set DJANGO_DEBUG=0 and APP_UID/APP_GID (`id -u`, `id -g`).
`mkdir -p data db` (to keep existing users: `cp db.sqlite3 db/`).
`docker compose up -d --build` starts the dashboard at http://127.0.0.1:8000 and the collector, which runs `./run.sh` every 3 hours (see `crontab`).
Create a user: `docker compose exec web python manage.py createsuperuser`.
Logs: `docker compose logs web`, collector runs in `data/*/log`.
